{"parentUuid":null,"isSidechain":false,"userType":"external","cwd":"/Users/demo/code/glasshouse","sessionId":"b98add6c-d29a-450a-b527-8ae38b417b93","version":"2.1.20","gitBranch":"main","entrypoint":"cli","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":"thinking about the hardware for glasshouse v2. esp32-c3 or pico w for the soil sensor nodes?"},"uuid":"8208b95b-41cf-47f1-ad11-1e0d02631a1f","timestamp":"2026-08-28T15:01:28.400Z"}
{"parentUuid":"8208b95b-41cf-47f1-ad11-1e0d02631a1f","isSidechain":false,"userType":"external","cwd":"/Users/demo/code/glasshouse","sessionId":"b98add6c-d29a-450a-b527-8ae38b417b93","version":"2.1.20","gitBranch":"main","entrypoint":"cli","type":"assistant","requestId":"req_1f64b30e5b627e5a1b0426b6","message":{"id":"msg_f2fa5c0f0b08872a6cf1bd1f","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"claude-opus-5-5","content":[{"type":"text","text":"ESP32-C3. Its deep sleep draws about 5 µA against the Pico W's roughly 1.3 mA dormant with Wi-Fi state kept, which is the difference between a year on two AA cells and a few weeks. The Pico W is nicer to program, but battery nodes live or die on sleep current."}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","usage":{"input_tokens":1240,"output_tokens":83}},"uuid":"a1587abc-8773-4901-9cef-8ccd952bfe84","timestamp":"2026-08-28T15:02:05.100Z"}
{"parentUuid":"a1587abc-8773-4901-9cef-8ccd952bfe84","isSidechain":false,"userType":"external","cwd":"/Users/demo/code/glasshouse","sessionId":"b98add6c-d29a-450a-b527-8ae38b417b93","version":"2.1.20","gitBranch":"main","entrypoint":"cli","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":"and capacitive vs resistive moisture probes"},"uuid":"649fe551-54b5-49aa-99b9-47875604bee1","timestamp":"2026-08-28T15:03:23.700Z"}
{"parentUuid":"649fe551-54b5-49aa-99b9-47875604bee1","isSidechain":false,"userType":"external","cwd":"/Users/demo/code/glasshouse","sessionId":"b98add6c-d29a-450a-b527-8ae38b417b93","version":"2.1.20","gitBranch":"main","entrypoint":"cli","type":"assistant","requestId":"req_5e27b23979af3574e3d15714","message":{"id":"msg_8c4f02945a70061b28772e61","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"claude-opus-5-5","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Capacitive. Resistive probes electrolyse and corrode within a season, and their readings drift as they do. Buy capacitive v2.0 boards and check that the 555 timer is the TLC555, since the cheap NE555 clones need 5 V."}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","usage":{"input_tokens":1320,"output_tokens":89}},"uuid":"d2d82451-b5a4-4fee-a1cb-a063849a54b7","timestamp":"2026-08-28T15:03:58.420Z"}
{"parentUuid":"d2d82451-b5a4-4fee-a1cb-a063849a54b7","isSidechain":false,"userType":"external","cwd":"/Users/demo/code/glasshouse","sessionId":"b98add6c-d29a-450a-b527-8ae38b417b93","version":"2.1.20","gitBranch":"main","entrypoint":"cli","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":"how many nodes for 12 beds"},"uuid":"0da60e2c-b05a-4149-b328-109219fb40cb","timestamp":"2026-08-28T15:05:13.620Z"}
{"parentUuid":"0da60e2c-b05a-4149-b328-109219fb40cb","isSidechain":false,"userType":"external","cwd":"/Users/demo/code/glasshouse","sessionId":"b98add6c-d29a-450a-b527-8ae38b417b93","version":"2.1.20","gitBranch":"main","entrypoint":"cli","type":"assistant","requestId":"req_972969a7f2ffadb9f6aa33d1","message":{"id":"msg_19e404ac4e5dfb8a4b74cef9","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"claude-opus-5-5","content":[{"type":"text","text":"One node per bed pair (six nodes) if the beds are adjacent, since each C3 has enough ADC channels for two probes. Put the air temperature and humidity sensor on a seventh node at bench height, away from the glazing."}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","usage":{"input_tokens":1400,"output_tokens":95}},"uuid":"6e4afcaf-ba12-4e32-ad39-1bbd09739e57","timestamp":"2026-08-28T15:05:48.295Z"}
{"parentUuid":"6e4afcaf-ba12-4e32-ad39-1bbd09739e57","isSidechain":false,"userType":"external","cwd":"/Users/demo/code/glasshouse","sessionId":"b98add6c-d29a-450a-b527-8ae38b417b93","version":"2.1.20","gitBranch":"main","entrypoint":"cli","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":"ok six plus one. what about calibration"},"uuid":"7fdd79a3-028a-4979-874b-8b932bb63430","timestamp":"2026-08-28T15:07:06.095Z"}
{"parentUuid":"7fdd79a3-028a-4979-874b-8b932bb63430","isSidechain":false,"userType":"external","cwd":"/Users/demo/code/glasshouse","sessionId":"b98add6c-d29a-450a-b527-8ae38b417b93","version":"2.1.20","gitBranch":"main","entrypoint":"cli","type":"assistant","requestId":"req_45975a23a3e04b303dd41fa8","message":{"id":"msg_33bf8e94c4f046069df3cba6","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"claude-opus-5-5","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Two-point per probe: read it in dry air, then in a glass of water, and store both in the node config. Moisture percent is then a linear map between the two, which is good enough for irrigation decisions."}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","usage":{"input_tokens":1480,"output_tokens":101}},"uuid":"f21cb410-7bc8-4d1f-9c2a-d104c881b9fe","timestamp":"2026-08-28T15:07:40.230Z"}
{"parentUuid":"f21cb410-7bc8-4d1f-9c2a-d104c881b9fe","isSidechain":false,"userType":"external","cwd":"/Users/demo/code/glasshouse","sessionId":"b98add6c-d29a-450a-b527-8ae38b417b93","version":"2.1.20","gitBranch":"main","entrypoint":"cli","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":"alerts next. I got woken up twice last week by frost alerts that were just one bad reading"},"uuid":"cd653558-45fe-4fdb-8ea6-c953e3496e0d","timestamp":"2026-08-28T17:39:08.230Z"}
{"parentUuid":"cd653558-45fe-4fdb-8ea6-c953e3496e0d","isSidechain":false,"userType":"external","cwd":"/Users/demo/code/glasshouse","sessionId":"b98add6c-d29a-450a-b527-8ae38b417b93","version":"2.1.20","gitBranch":"main","entrypoint":"cli","type":"assistant","requestId":"req_c53ee2348f08a2d20208ee8c","message":{"id":"msg_fe925c8b0dd76202057628c7","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"claude-opus-5-5","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Alert on a condition held over time, not a single sample: frost when temperature stays below 2 °C for 10 minutes. Add hysteresis so it clears only above 3 °C, otherwise a reading hovering at 2.0 flaps the alert on and off."}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","usage":{"input_tokens":1560,"output_tokens":107}},"uuid":"ed98640a-29f1-4fcf-99bf-bc5f29fea6ac","timestamp":"2026-08-28T17:39:43.220Z"}
{"parentUuid":"ed98640a-29f1-4fcf-99bf-bc5f29fea6ac","isSidechain":false,"userType":"external","cwd":"/Users/demo/code/glasshouse","sessionId":"b98add6c-d29a-450a-b527-8ae38b417b93","version":"2.1.20","gitBranch":"main","entrypoint":"cli","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":"what about when a node goes silent"},"uuid":"c8ef3cad-88e7-45d3-b3af-c705f1a06215","timestamp":"2026-08-28T17:41:00.020Z"}
{"parentUuid":"c8ef3cad-88e7-45d3-b3af-c705f1a06215","isSidechain":false,"userType":"external","cwd":"/Users/demo/code/glasshouse","sessionId":"b98add6c-d29a-450a-b527-8ae38b417b93","version":"2.1.20","gitBranch":"main","entrypoint":"cli","type":"assistant","requestId":"req_49721ad738d15627e73f0915","message":{"id":"msg_258be040282906b5e661d56e","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"claude-opus-5-5","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Treat silence as its own alert with a longer window: no reading from a node for 30 minutes means \"node offline,\" which is different from \"frost.\" Sleeping nodes report every 5 minutes, so 30 minutes is six missed check-ins."}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","usage":{"input_tokens":1640,"output_tokens":113}},"uuid":"d90d7004-d944-445b-98cb-766e30b1edea","timestamp":"2026-08-28T17:41:35.055Z"}
{"parentUuid":"d90d7004-d944-445b-98cb-766e30b1edea","isSidechain":false,"userType":"external","cwd":"/Users/demo/code/glasshouse","sessionId":"b98add6c-d29a-450a-b527-8ae38b417b93","version":"2.1.20","gitBranch":"main","entrypoint":"cli","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":"should alerts go to my phone or just the dashboard"},"uuid":"5b7ea422-cbdf-435c-9e62-6cde35bd1c25","timestamp":"2026-08-28T17:42:55.055Z"}
{"parentUuid":"5b7ea422-cbdf-435c-9e62-6cde35bd1c25","isSidechain":false,"userType":"external","cwd":"/Users/demo/code/glasshouse","sessionId":"b98add6c-d29a-450a-b527-8ae38b417b93","version":"2.1.20","gitBranch":"main","entrypoint":"cli","type":"assistant","requestId":"req_4e0f8507ce81a2b457b671d5","message":{"id":"msg_1739c61e869ad693eec9671f","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"claude-opus-5-5","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Phone for frost and node-offline, dashboard only for everything else. The rule of thumb: page for things that need action within the hour."}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","usage":{"input_tokens":1720,"output_tokens":119}},"uuid":"83e6095b-3779-46f8-9da3-203e3796f63f","timestamp":"2026-08-28T17:43:26.265Z"}
{"parentUuid":"83e6095b-3779-46f8-9da3-203e3796f63f","isSidechain":false,"userType":"external","cwd":"/Users/demo/code/glasshouse","sessionId":"b98add6c-d29a-450a-b527-8ae38b417b93","version":"2.1.20","gitBranch":"main","entrypoint":"cli","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":"makes sense, frost can kill seedlings overnight"},"uuid":"0d5246f7-6c81-4a06-94d6-36ebfed67a15","timestamp":"2026-08-28T17:44:45.665Z"}
{"parentUuid":"0d5246f7-6c81-4a06-94d6-36ebfed67a15","isSidechain":false,"userType":"external","cwd":"/Users/demo/code/glasshouse","sessionId":"b98add6c-d29a-450a-b527-8ae38b417b93","version":"2.1.20","gitBranch":"main","entrypoint":"cli","type":"assistant","requestId":"req_7337e3a97767c851e9e7755d","message":{"id":"msg_d6721e7e721391dd3318d48c","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"claude-opus-5-5","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Exactly. Frost and offline page you; dry-soil and high-humidity just colour the bed tile."}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","usage":{"input_tokens":1800,"output_tokens":125}},"uuid":"6d72b922-f15a-4e9f-b7dd-bce6779fa86f","timestamp":"2026-08-28T17:45:14.670Z"}
{"parentUuid":"6d72b922-f15a-4e9f-b7dd-bce6779fa86f","isSidechain":false,"userType":"external","cwd":"/Users/demo/code/glasshouse","sessionId":"b98add6c-d29a-450a-b527-8ae38b417b93","version":"2.1.20","gitBranch":"main","entrypoint":"cli","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":"totally different question, my tomatoes have blossom end rot again. is that watering?"},"uuid":"9b2a0255-f557-41ac-a903-7982c3f6e5d9","timestamp":"2026-08-28T21:06:41.670Z"}
{"parentUuid":"9b2a0255-f557-41ac-a903-7982c3f6e5d9","isSidechain":false,"userType":"external","cwd":"/Users/demo/code/glasshouse","sessionId":"b98add6c-d29a-450a-b527-8ae38b417b93","version":"2.1.20","gitBranch":"main","entrypoint":"cli","type":"assistant","requestId":"req_796598ee11b2aa59ad76c95b","message":{"id":"msg_d03c36f44c2b6d5bf6d758c9","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"claude-opus-5-5","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Usually, yes. Blossom end rot is a calcium delivery problem, and it's most often caused by uneven watering rather than too little calcium in the soil. Swings between dry and soaked stop calcium reaching the fruit."}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","usage":{"input_tokens":1880,"output_tokens":131}},"uuid":"f5cd60ff-d94e-4ebe-b463-0480e88a6115","timestamp":"2026-08-28T21:07:16.255Z"}
{"parentUuid":"f5cd60ff-d94e-4ebe-b463-0480e88a6115","isSidechain":false,"userType":"external","cwd":"/Users/demo/code/glasshouse","sessionId":"b98add6c-d29a-450a-b527-8ae38b417b93","version":"2.1.20","gitBranch":"main","entrypoint":"cli","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":"could glasshouse run a drip valve to keep it even"},"uuid":"1e93d39c-0763-4acc-a21f-da69cb7fdf45","timestamp":"2026-08-28T21:08:36.055Z"}
{"parentUuid":"1e93d39c-0763-4acc-a21f-da69cb7fdf45","isSidechain":false,"userType":"external","cwd":"/Users/demo/code/glasshouse","sessionId":"b98add6c-d29a-450a-b527-8ae38b417b93","version":"2.1.20","gitBranch":"main","entrypoint":"cli","type":"assistant","requestId":"req_641a485502e54b0046a1a205","message":{"id":"msg_35e256881785fc841dae39ee","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"claude-opus-5-5","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Yes. A 12 V solenoid valve on a relay from one node, opened when the bed's moisture drops below its threshold and closed after a fixed volume. Cap it at a few cycles per day so a failed probe can't flood the bed."}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","usage":{"input_tokens":1960,"output_tokens":137}},"uuid":"b4e073f5-6a2c-49e3-83e5-36c14c48bec7","timestamp":"2026-08-28T21:09:10.595Z"}
{"parentUuid":"b4e073f5-6a2c-49e3-83e5-36c14c48bec7","isSidechain":false,"userType":"external","cwd":"/Users/demo/code/glasshouse","sessionId":"b98add6c-d29a-450a-b527-8ae38b417b93","version":"2.1.20","gitBranch":"main","entrypoint":"cli","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":"what threshold for tomatoes"},"uuid":"d1a09cd6-e0e1-48f5-aefe-541321682cae","timestamp":"2026-08-28T21:10:25.995Z"}
{"parentUuid":"d1a09cd6-e0e1-48f5-aefe-541321682cae","isSidechain":false,"userType":"external","cwd":"/Users/demo/code/glasshouse","sessionId":"b98add6c-d29a-450a-b527-8ae38b417b93","version":"2.1.20","gitBranch":"main","entrypoint":"cli","type":"assistant","requestId":"req_2a9faa93acf22fc0b7c59eef","message":{"id":"msg_aab8abc7ef59d73ae2acf91d","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"claude-opus-5-5","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Start by opening the valve at 35% and stopping at 50% on your calibrated scale, then adjust by how the soil feels at finger depth for a week."}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","usage":{"input_tokens":2040,"output_tokens":143}},"uuid":"907e1051-6ec4-4f6a-9370-113cc1552978","timestamp":"2026-08-28T21:10:57.340Z"}
{"parentUuid":"907e1051-6ec4-4f6a-9370-113cc1552978","isSidechain":false,"userType":"external","cwd":"/Users/demo/code/glasshouse","sessionId":"b98add6c-d29a-450a-b527-8ae38b417b93","version":"2.1.20","gitBranch":"main","entrypoint":"cli","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":"ordering a valve tonight"},"uuid":"d436c4f5-c2ee-4652-9f95-e6df66cb22b2","timestamp":"2026-08-28T21:12:12.140Z"}
